edition 5;

module skillc;

// `table skill`: the compact profile (docs/agent-cost.md section 4, issue #105). About 2 KB, leading with `--query`, for a model that reads it before its first call. The exhaustive text, which the contract
// package generates from the flag table and the rule table, is `table skill --full`. This one is written by hand, and the tests hold it to the tool: its size (`test_skill.Compact`), every flag and rule
// tag it names (they exist in `introspect`), and every command in it (run on a fixture, the answer or the refusal it says).
pub fn text() -> [] &static [byte] {
    return "# table 0.3.0\n\nA CSV, TSV or JSON-lines file as a table. One JSON line comes back (schema table.v2), or a refusal: error.rule says which, error.hint how to fix it, error.repair what to run. It reads under --root and writes nothing.\n\nAsk in SQL or in flags; both give the same bytes. On sales.csv (host,status,bytes,price):\n\n  table --query \"select host, count(*) from 'sales.csv' where status = 200 group by host order by count(*) desc limit 5\"\n  table --select host,bytes --where 'status = 200' --order-by -bytes:int --limit 5 sales.csv\n  table --group host --agg count,sum:bytes --sort -count --top 5 sales.csv\n  table --join hosts.csv --on host --join-type left --join-prefix h_ sales.csv\n  table --report types sales.csv\n  table --explain --select host sales.csv\n\nOne form per call: the shape (FILE alone), rows (--select, --where, --order-by), groups (--group, --agg), a join (--join, --on) or the type report (--report types). A mix is args.conflict. --explain with any of them prints the plan and runs nothing.\n\nWHERE: COLUMN OP VALUE with OP one of = != < <= > >= contains; COLUMN in (a, b); not (...); and or or, never both at one level (use parentheses).\n\nTypes: a column is text, compared bytewise, unless you write its type: COLUMN:int, :dec(S) (exact, S fractional digits), :float, :date, :timestamp, :datetime. 10 sorts before 9 as text. A cell that is not of its type is refused (value.not-integer and its kin), and so is an empty one: keep it out first, --where \"n != '' and n:int > 5\".\n\nA page is 1000 rows: --limit N, --from N, and data.next.from says where the next one starts.\n\nA repair of kind retry is an argv to run as it is; choose lists options; none says why there is none.\n\nEvery flag, rule and limit: table skill --full, or table introspect.\n";
}
